BrianHShen@gmail.com wrote:
> To have my pet steal, do I just stand in the block directly outside the
> door and keep waiting until he drops something either in the door or in
> the first square inside? I have a lot of trouble getting my money/items
> from a store by using my pet.

When I don't have a leash/magic whistle/tripe to train the pet then
here's my steal method:

1. Drop the pile of gold to the right/left of the dorway (immediately
besides the shopkeeper)
2. Move to the doorway and start waiting.

Your pet should circle the square in front of you, the pile square and
maybe a few others.

4. Wait until your pet picks up the item.

Now comes the tricky part.  Instead of just standing still and hoping
that the pet drops the item directly in front of you, on the only
square in the shop that the shopkeeper doesn't "own", you try to lead
your pet outside.  This takes some practice, but isn't that hard when
you get the hang of it.

At first, just try to walk away from the shop and see if your pet
follows.  If it does, then great.  Just let it catch up with you, and
then displace it so that you are standing between it and the shop
entrance.  In a few turns it will drop the gold pile for you to pick
up.

A better method is waiting so that the pet has direct line of sight on
you.  Let the pet pick up the gold, wait one turn and see if it moves
in a space that is directly in front of you, then start moving away
from the shop.

You have to make sure that the shopkeeper doesn't move in front of the
pet while you're leading it.  If he does, then you'll probably have to
start over.

Just keep trying and with practice it will start to work better.

NB.  This is based on experimentation, not on any source diving.  I do
not know exactly how the pet AI works, but this method seems to work
for me.

